WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.034
The walkdown starts with equipment
identity,

2
00:00:03.155 --> 00:00:05.361
not a copied supplier checklist.

3
00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:08.447
Compare the vessel tag, manufacturer
model,

4
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.360
serial number and location with the
controlled package.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.652
A matching tag attached to a different
vessel would not establish identity.

6
00:00:17.773 --> 00:00:22.048
Record discrepancies individually so a
later reviewer can tell

7
00:00:22.168 --> 00:00:25.962
which identifiers matched and which
remained uncertain.

8
00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:30.306
Work through the installed arrangement
systematically.

9
00:00:30.426 --> 00:00:34.977
Identify the agitator assembly and
supports, then trace the outlet

10
00:00:35.097 --> 00:00:38.959
and instrument connections against the
relevant drawing.

11
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.792
Confirm required orientation and
accessible features

12
00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.912
using the approved method.

13
00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:48.894
Do not run the agitator to infer
installation conformity

14
00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:52.600
when the authorized activity is a static
inspection.

15
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.789
Functional rotation checks belong in the
defined test plan.

16
00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:01.961
The design allowed a rear instrument to
slide out for maintenance,

17
00:01:02.081 --> 00:01:06.081
but the installed pipe rack crosses that
removal envelope.

18
00:01:06.201 --> 00:01:09.374
A front-facing photograph misses this
problem.

19
00:01:09.494 --> 00:01:11.494
Compare the full maintenance

20
00:01:11.614 --> 00:01:16.372
envelope with the approved arrangement and
manufacturer requirements.

21
00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:19.251
No universal clearance is supplied here.

22
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:22.475
Document the obstruction and its
consequences

23
00:01:22.595 --> 00:01:25.667
without inventing a numerical GMP minimum.

24
00:01:26.287 --> 00:01:30.287
A covered connection cannot be recorded as
verified solely

25
00:01:30.407 --> 00:01:32.476
because its neighbour matches.

26
00:01:32.596 --> 00:01:34.622
Record the inaccessible item,

27
00:01:34.742 --> 00:01:38.466
why it could not be examined and the
agreed follow-up.

28
00:01:38.586 --> 00:01:41.345
If suitable controlled evidence supports

29
00:01:41.465 --> 00:01:45.258
another verification method, justify its
applicability.

30
00:01:45.378 --> 00:01:48.898
Distinguish direct observation from
document review

31
00:01:49.018 --> 00:01:52.604
so the evidence does not appear stronger
than it is.
